# Billion Word Imputation — solution

Metric: mean character-level Levenshtein distance between submitted sentence and the original
sentence (lower is better). Test: 302,644 sentences with one interior word removed.

## Approach (final)
1. **Gap detector** — `roberta-base` encoder with two heads (gap / word), trained on `train_v2.txt`
   by masking exactly one random interior token per sentence (mimics the test hole). The gap head
   outputs a distribution over the `n-1` interior insertion slots; argmax = insertion position and
   max prob = confidence. Location precision ≈0.94 at ~77% coverage (τ=0.65) on a 30k holdout.
2. **Missing-word model** — masked-LM prediction at the chosen gap: `roberta-large` (optionally
   fine-tuned on `train_v2`, masked-word recipe). Word chosen by **expected character Levenshtein**
   over the top-k distribution (λ=0), which minimises expected edit distance under uncertainty.
3. **Selective insertion** — insert only if detector gap confidence ≥ τ=0.65, else leave the
   sentence unchanged. This is essential: a wrong-location insertion costs more than leaving the
   hole.
4. n-gram LM was explored (bigram/trigram counts, candidate generation + Levenshtein-aware
   refinement) but diagnostics showed it adds ~0 over detector+MLM after honest (leak-free)
   calibration, so it is **not** part of the final decision.

## Validation
- Holdout = last 30,000 train sentences, one random interior token removed (never first/last;
  deterministic seed). Baseline (no insertion) = 5.5465.
- n-gram counts for calibration were rebuilt **excluding** the holdout (leak-free).
- Holdout metric of the pipeline: see `METRICS.md`.

## External models (all general-purpose pretrained, not competition-specific)
| model | HF id | revision | license | purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| RoBERTa base | `roberta-base` | `e2da8e2f811d1448a5b465c236feacd80ffbac7b` | MIT | detector encoder (re-initialised heads, trained on train_v2 only) |
| RoBERTa large | `roberta-large` | `722cf37b1afa9454edce342e7895e588b6ff1d59` | MIT | MLM word prediction at chosen gap; optionally fine-tuned on train_v2 |

No competition test labels were used anywhere; validation only on a holdout cut from `train_v2.txt`.

## Reproduce
- `code/`: training/inference scripts (detector, MLM word model, submission writer).
- `submission.csv`: predictions for `data/test_v2.txt` (ids 0..302643).
