   prefixes + a small set of common words; choose the string minimizing the expected character
   Levenshtein distance to the word posterior with a length weight λ=0.05. (Because the metric is
   character-level, a shared-prefix hedge such as "th" can be strictly better in expectation than
   committing to a full word when the model is uncertain.)
4. Insert only where detector confidence ≥ 0.60.

